  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  Optional. Pre-grants the runtime permissions Android Auto asks for, so that
  first connection in a moving car is not eight consecutive dialogs.

  All entries are fixed="false", which means the user can revoke every one of
  them afterwards in Settings. A fixed="true" grant cannot be revoked, and
  nothing here justifies that.

  THE CERTIFICATE DIGEST IS DELIBERATELY LEFT BLANK.

  <exception> matches on package name AND on the SHA-256 digest of the signing
  certificate, so that a default grant cannot be captured by a same-named
  package signed by somebody else. Filling it in means stating the fingerprint
  of a specific Google-signed build of Android Auto -- and which build that is,
  is precisely the decision this repository refuses to make on anyone's behalf
  (see README.md, and docs/07-provenance.md for the general rule).

  Whoever ships the placeholder APK already has the file. Read the digest off
  the one they chose:

      apksigner verify --print-certs AndroidAutoPlaceholder.apk

  and paste the SHA-256 line, colon-separated and upper case, below. A wrong
  or absent digest is not dangerous: the exception simply never matches and
  the user is prompted normally, which is the pre-2020 behaviour and is fine.

  If in doubt, ship without this file at all. It is a convenience, not a
  requirement, and it is the one file here that encodes a trust decision.
-->
<exceptions>
    <exception
            package="com.google.android.projection.gearhead"
            sha256-cert-digest="FILL_IN_FROM_THE_APK_YOU_SHIP">

        <!-- Turn-by-turn on the head unit, and the car's own position feed. -->
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>

        <!-- Dialling and caller ID on the car screen. -->
        <permission name="android.permission.CALL_PHONE" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_PHONE_STATE" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_CONTACTS" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_CALL_LOG" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.WRITE_CALL_LOG" fixed="false"/>

        <!-- Message notification read-out and reply. Note that without the
             Google app there is no assistant to dictate a reply to, so the
             SMS grants buy less on a de-Googled phone than on a stock one.
             They are the first candidates to drop. -->
        <permission name="android.permission.RECEIVE_SMS" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_SMS" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.SEND_SMS" fixed="false"/>

        <!-- Microphone. Also of reduced use with no assistant; keep it only if
             the head unit's voice button is expected to do anything. -->
        <permission name="android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO" fixed="false"/>

    </exception>
</exceptions>
